# Keep the build context small and the image honest.
.git
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache

# 224 MB of Sintel master, and the 240 MB of content-addressed media derived
# from it. A container is the wrong place for a film. The Dockerfile copies
# only the small half of the store -- index, QC reports, ledger, metadata --
# which is what the control room needs to show real lineage.
assets/sintel
bin

# Never ship credentials in a layer.
.env.local
.env

# Never ship credentials in a layer.
.gcp-continuity.json
.cloudrun-env.yaml

# Not needed at runtime. scripts/ IS needed: the control room's approve button
# runs scripts/repair.py rather than reimplementing a repair.
tests
# The screenshots are served by the control room from its own origin,
# so they have to be in the image. The rest of docs/ is prose.
docs/*
!docs/img/
!docs/gallery/
deploy
grafana/rules/tests

# out/ is a scratch directory that also happens to hold the asset store, so it
# is excluded wholesale and the four things the image genuinely needs are named
# back in. An allowlist because the denylist form already failed once: a new
# out/probe/ appeared holding an 85 MB wav and went straight into the build
# context, because a filter can only exclude the directories it was told about.
out/*
!out/store/
# ...but not the media inside it. Only these two are large: objects/ is 245 MB
# of content-addressed audio and tts/ is the synthesis cache. Everything else in
# the store totals about 180 KB and is exactly what the control room needs to
# show real lineage, real QC and a real repair history.
#
# Named as two exclusions rather than a list of four things to keep, because the
# allowlist form silently dropped out/store/forced_narrative.json the moment it
# appeared -- and the release check that reads it concluded, correctly and
# uselessly, that nobody had analysed the picture for on-screen text. A market
# was blocked by a packaging rule. The store is ours and its shape is known, so
# excluding the two big directories is safe where a blanket denylist over out/
# was not.
out/store/objects/
out/store/tts/
# The scene the technical checks probe. 3.7 MB, and without it the hosted
# exporter can republish every measurement that lives in a QC report but not
# the ones that come from looking at the file itself -- so resolution, frame
# rate, codec and pixel format would read as never-measured, and every market
# would be blocked for a reason that was an artefact of packaging.
!out/scenes/
out/scenes/*
!out/scenes/S03.mp4
!out/scenes/manifest.json
# The produced media itself: dubs, described tracks, subtitles and the packaged
# deliverables. About 30 MB, and the reason the hosted control room can PLAY
# what the agents made rather than only describe it. A dub you cannot hear is
# indistinguishable from one that was never made, and a deployed service that
# lists four outputs and plays none of them is exactly that.
!out/ad/
!out/dub/
!out/subs/
!out/deliverables/
# NOT the scene's own audio, which every market's "original" output resolves
# to and which lives in objects/. Two attempts to re-include that one file
# past the exclusion of the directory holding it were refused by the upload
# filter -- correctly, by gitignore's own rule that a file cannot be put back
# once its parent directory is out. So the hosted control room plays the dub,
# the described track and the packaged deliverable, and simply does not list
# an original it has no bytes for. `outputs` omits what is not there rather
# than offering a control that cannot play.

